WF-12 — Admin → WhatsApp Relay

## Summary

- Inputs: From caller: {phoneNumber, messageText, botMessage (bool)}
- Outputs: WhatsApp text message sent to the user via WF-50
- State Transitions: none
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-50 (Send WhatsApp)
- **Ambiguities / Notes:**
  - **Likely legacy / dead workflow.** No caller currently routes to WF-12 per WF-10's dispatch graph — the active admin→user relay runs through WF-41. Inputs (`botMessage`, `messageText`) are inferred from this workflow's filter conditions, not from any live caller.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by another workflow (intended caller: a Slack-side relay path) with {phoneNumber, messageText, botMessage}.
Step 2: Filter — keep only items where:
  - botMessage != true (drop bot-originated messages), AND
  - messageText does NOT start with '/' (drop slash-commands).
  If the item fails either condition → drop, End.
Step 3: Call WF-50 (Send WhatsApp) with {phoneNumber: <phoneNumber>, messageBody: <messageText>}.
Step 4: End.

Note: This workflow appears to be a thin/legacy passthrough; the active admin→user relay path goes through WF-41 (per WF-10). WF-12 is included in the registry but only does a filter + WF-50 send.
